## 2. Framework Decision

**Selected Framework:** Anthropic Python SDK v0.28+ (direct tool-calling via messages API)

**Version:** anthropic>=0.28.0,<2.0.0 (already in requirements.txt)

**Rationale:**
The Anthropic SDK is already declared in backend/requirements.txt and AnthropicProvider in backend/ai_providers.py already hits the /v1/messages endpoint via httpx. Phase 12 only requires extending AnthropicProvider.generate() to accept a `tools` parameter and parse `tool_use` content blocks — a surgical addition to one method with zero new dependencies. The circuit-breaker, MockProvider fallback, and ai_audit_logs infrastructure already satisfy the graceful-degradation and audit requirements without any additional framework.

**Alternatives Considered:**

| Framework | Ruled Out Because |
|-----------|------------------|
| LangGraph | Phase 12 is a single-model, single-turn tool-selection loop — graph state machine and checkpointing machinery add significant scaffolding for what is effectively one new method on an already-wired provider class |
| CrewAI | Multi-agent orchestration — Phase 12 needs a single LLM making one tool-calling decision per agentic task, not a crew of specialized agents |

**Vendor Lock-In Accepted:** Yes — Anthropic-only (claude-sonnet-4-6 is the specified model); MockProvider fallback ensures CI and offline resilience.

